# Tier 3 (the reasoning tier) calls a model through /api/reconcile.
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill ONE of the keys below.
# .env.local is gitignored — never put a real key in this file.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Groq — https://console.groq.com/keys
# Free tier available. Uses openai/gpt-oss-120b, which supports strict
# json_schema decoding, so match decisions come back schema-validated.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Anthropic — https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Requires credit on the account. Uses claude-opus-5.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional.
#
# Which provider to use when both keys are set: groq | anthropic
# LEDGER_PROVIDER=groq
#
# Override the model. Groq strict-mode options: openai/gpt-oss-120b (default,
# stronger) or openai/gpt-oss-20b (faster).
# LEDGER_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
#
# Dollars per million tokens, for the cost meter. Anthropic rates are built in.
# Groq does not publish a machine-readable price list, so set these to see cost
# in dollars — otherwise the meter reports tokens and latency only.
# Current rates: https://groq.com/pricing
# LEDGER_PRICE_IN=0.15
# LEDGER_PRICE_OUT=0.75
